  "id": "ch2",
  "title": "THE CORAL CAUSEWAY",
  "objPage": "S3A0",
  "preset": "coral",
  "notes": [
    "CAMPAIGN.md §6.1 / §12.2 '2-1'..'2-6'. The drive (a0 = S1-S3, a2 = S6) is the HELL ROAD loop E3a0 15872-19712 (the ROM's own repeat, period 3840 = 0xF00) under the coral palette; a1 (S4-S5) is on foot.",
    "The causeway: the far edge of the HELL ROAD ground (y 128-160) is sea in every column of the loop: E6a1 open-water cells (E6a1 2688-3008, h 304-336, palette row 20, dimmed to the dusk), every other 320-px copy mirrored so the copies meet on mirror joins; the HELL ROAD mesas (scroll3) now stand in the sea as coral stacks. The road itself (y 160-224, the drive band) keeps the coral-tinted sand.",
    "2-6 THE RISING TIDE (CAMPAIGN 2-6, PLAN R7): the tide is one row higher and has crossed the far edge of the road (water at y 112-176, four cells; the drive band stays 161-224, the car wades at the top of it): 960 of the 3360 loop cells (28.6 %) are patched, over the non-identity coral palette. The loop's wrap copy (x 3840-4224) repeats x 0-384 exactly, patches included, so nothing pops in when the road wraps.",
    "Gate 4 takes the loop exemption (user question 5 default) only for the boss window: the loop content repeats into the original HELL ROAD boss window at 32752 (reported as a warning); every loop column is patched, so no verbatim run remains.",
    "The coral preset's ops are all row-role ops; the drive areas give explicit row ops instead (E3a0 scroll2 row 2 = the sand: hue -12 and 16% toward #d98a8a, coral flats; scroll3 row 4 = the mesas: 30% toward #d98a8a, coral stacks; row 5 = the dusk sky: 18% toward #3a5a9a, sea light), so no piece keeps the original palette.",
    "2-5: E6a0 864-1120 (CAMPAIGN) has no floor at 848-944 (the propped portal pillar comes down to the bottom of the screen: terrain types 6/7 only), so the gatehouse is E6a0 576-832 (the village wall and hut just before the portal); the portal's timber post (E6a0 864-896, rows 9/8/3/2 lifted off the rock face) is the toll post that covers every join of a1 (CAMPAIGN §4.1 join chunks).",
    "Far layer: the drive uses E3a0's periodic scroll3 (X3 2304-2560 repeats every 256 px, map3Entry wrap at 0xA00) sampled at mod((cam.x + road) >> 3, 256); a1 has one far layer per section (2-4 E6a0, 2-5 E5a0), changing under the toll post at 1024."
  ],
